2. Abstract

Abstract (sample):This white sheet presents a conceptual design for a Hamiltonian‑coupled, multi‑physics simulator that fuses biological fluid dynamics and astrophysical flux fields into a unified cryptographic entropy engine. Biological state vectors ((q_{bio}, p_{bio})) and astrophysical FITS cube data are integrated into a port‑Hamiltonian system whose chaotic divergence, monitored via Lyapunov exponents, is used to derive non‑deterministic encryption keys. The resulting architecture—termed the Blackwell Encryption Layer (BEL)—implements physics‑verified key generation and XOR‑based ciphering over an encrypted simulation stream. This document formalizes the design rationale, mathematical framework, and implementation pathway for future validation and experimental realization.

